# ==== T-FMT-B — SYNONYM (Q3 PRESERVE): the two `await` spellings.
# SCOPE CLAIM: `Expr::Await` rendering. Gorget accepts prefix `await e` and
# postfix `e.await()`; both build the SAME `Expr::Await` node, so the choice is
# authorial information the AST must now carry (`prefix_form`), exactly like a
# literal's radix.
# Pre-fix RED (measured): every prefix `await f()` was rewritten to
# `f().await()` — a whole-file rewrite of any codebase that prefers the prefix
# spelling.
async int f():
    return 1

async void g():
    int a = await f()
    int b = f().await()
    print(a + b)

async void main():
    await g()
